# roam-269: chrome://flags/#roamux-refresh-all-initial-urls — the kill-switch for
# kRefreshAllInitialUrls. Structural precedent: patch 0064 (roam-266).
#
# This patch is NOT optional polish; it is what makes 0065 admissible. Since
# roam-226 every Roamux flag ships default-ON with an opt-out entry in the SAME
# change. kRefreshAllInitialUrls ships on, so without this row it would be the
# only default-on Roamux feature a user cannot turn off — and, unlike a
# staged-rollout flag, it is live for every user of the next build the moment it
# merges.
#
# THREE files, matching 0064 exactly — and note what is NOT here:
#   1. chrome/browser/about_flags.cc — one FeatureEntry with the name and
#      description INLINED. The overlay has no roamux-owned flag-descriptions
#      unit and 0064 set the precedent of inlining; routing through
#      flag_descriptions.{h,cc} would add TWO more upstream files to the patch
#      surface for no gain. (The roam-269 issue text asked for
#      flag_descriptions.{h,cc}; that was wrong in both directions — it also
#      omitted flag-never-expire-list.json below.)
#   2. chrome/browser/flag-metadata.json — the row, in GLOBAL ALPHABETICAL
#      ORDER (between roamux-initial-url and roamux-signin-opt-in), owner set,
#      expiry_milestone -1.
#   3. chrome/browser/flag-never-expire-list.json — REQUIRED by expiry -1.
#      AboutFlagsTest enforces `expiry -1 subset-of never-expire-list`; omitting
#      this is a silent failure everywhere except that test.
#
# kOsMac only: Roamux is a macOS-only target (plan §7.1), and the chord is
# dispatched through the mac shortcut registry.
#
# CI-INVISIBLE GATE: AboutFlagsTest lives in `unit_tests`, NOT in any roamux
# target, and tier-2 does not run it. It enforces the global alphabetical order
# and the never-expire invariant above. A malformed entry here passes lint,
# governance, targeted-suite, tier-2 and every check on the PR — while leaving a
# default-on feature with no working opt-out. Run it locally on any change to
# these three files (needs DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH for Sparkle).
#
# Flag-off behaviour (what the user gets by toggling this): the registry drops
# the Ctrl+Opt+Cmd+R row, CommandForChord returns -1 so the chord is unclaimed
# and falls through to stock handling, CanRefreshAllInitialUrls returns false so
# the command is disabled, and roam-270's submenu item disappears with the rest
# of the submenu. Nothing is stranded.
diff --git a/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc b/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc
index 0ace70696f..e111777e39 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc
@@ -4755,6 +4755,19 @@ const FeatureEntry kFeatureEntries[] = {
      "Chromium profile and sign-in behaviour.",
      kOsMac | kOsWin | kOsLinux,
      FEATURE_VALUE_TYPE(roamux::features::kBraveStyleProfiles)},
+    // Roamux (roam-269): the refresh-all-initial-URLs command. Ships default-on
+    // like every Roamux flag since roam-226, so this entry IS the kill-switch
+    // and lands in the same change as the feature (the roam-266 precedent —
+    // without it this would be the only default-on Roamux flag a user cannot
+    // turn off). Turning it off unclaims Ctrl+Opt+Cmd+R entirely: the registry
+    // drops its row and CommandForChord returns -1, so the chord falls through
+    // to stock behaviour.
+    {"roamux-refresh-all-initial-urls", "Roamux: refresh all initial URLs",
+     "Adds Ctrl+Opt+Cmd+R, which reloads every tab in the window to its initial "
+     "URL, started one at a time rather than all at once. Turn this off to "
+     "remove the shortcut and the tab-menu item.",
+     kOsMac,
+     FEATURE_VALUE_TYPE(roamux::features::kRefreshAllInitialUrls)},
     // Roamux (roam-31): developer mirror of
     // roamux.signin.optional_entry_point_enabled (E5). Functional sign-in
     // additionally requires a keyed-and-authorized build (three-state
